From 723f40aa7c518e297625628615ee81a264dd1313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:26:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): route review_unpinned and non-fresh
 pins off a known quota wall before spawn

PR #1071 only moved base-tier `default` cards off a wall the host already
knows (provider_walls.json or the live pool). Two routes still spawned one
exit-75 run into it per card:

- Review lane: `review_unpinned` picked openai-codex while provider_walls.json
  held it for days (hub run 174730, card t_01a1c4799083f6b4).
  `resolve_dispatch_tier` now tries the other independent reviewers the
  resolver itself would choose (strong tier, then deep routes distinct from the
  implementer) and takes the first on an unwalled provider
  (`review_unpinned+wall:<provider>`). None free, or a `require_model: true`
  line: the route is kept, never a second wall. An active quota episode still
  decides first.
- Pinned cards: `kanban_pin_reroute` rule 1 accepted only the card's own wall
  or a live-pool wall on a fresh card, so a card woken from `scheduled` paid one
  wall run (MBP run 13181, t_c21c170e). Rule 1 now also accepts a wall the
  provider file or live pool knows on the pin's provider, fresh or not
  (`known_wall`). The other rules (min hours, non-mandatory, ready lane, one
  class, free peer) are unchanged; `record` reads the same wall for resets_at.

Tests: RED->GREEN for both gaps with controls (mandatory column and marker,
walled peer, near wall, no/walled alternative reviewer), plus the M2f mutant
test: a default card naming `require_model` in prose is still moved off a
walled default provider by `_class_alternate_off_wall`.
